# =============================================================================
# aura-backend .env  —  SAME FILE works for LOCAL and PRODUCTION.
#
# Setup (local machine AND server):   cp .env.example .env
#
# NODE_ENV is NOT set here on purpose:
#   local dev  -> `npm run dev`                                   (development)
#   production -> `pm2 start ecosystem.config.cjs --env production` (production)
#
# One backend serves BOTH sites by hostname (ag.* -> admin, else -> user),
# so there is only ONE port. Upload URLs auto-derive from the request and
# Cloudinary URLs are returned as-is, so no upload-host vars are needed.
# =============================================================================

